{
  "headline": "FDA's shortage list shows hydroxocobalamin injection from BTG International Inc. and Teva Pharmaceuticals USA, Inc. as Current since 2024-11-04",
  "headline_cites": ["E4", "E5"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's shortage list includes hydroxocobalamin injection from BTG International Inc. and Teva Pharmaceuticals USA, Inc., both listed as Current with initial posting on 2024-11-04.",
      "cites": ["E4", "E5"]
    },
    {
      "text": "As of 2026-10-21 the shortage has been on FDA's list for 24 months.",
      "cites": ["D3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our supply at both Corvale East and Corvale General is labeled by Actavis Pharma, Inc. (NDC 00591288830) and names Hikma Farmaceutica (Portugal) S.A. as the manufacturing plant on the label.",
      "cites": ["E1", "E2", "E3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no public FDA inspection signal (OAI, VAI, or NAI) for that plant in the evidence provided.",
      "cites": ["E3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East has 20 vials on hand at 3.9 vials per day, giving 5.1 days of supply.",
      "cites": ["D1"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale General has 75 vials on hand at 4 vials per day, giving 18.7 days of supply.",
      "cites": ["D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule‑ranked best option is to transfer 18 vials of 1000 ug/mL, 30 mL from Corvale General to Corvale East, which would leave Corvale General with about two weeks of supply and bring Corvale East to roughly 10 days.",
      "cites": ["D4"]
    }
  ]
}
